**Theorem 7.1 (complete names for the actual relation and its refinement).**
Fix $m\ge2,d\ge2,\ell\ge1$. Let $B_{m,d,\ell}\subseteq S_d^N$
be the complete actual relation of $\ell$ copies of $\mathcal T_{m,d}$,
where $N=11m\ell$ and $|B_{m,d,\ell}|=(2^m+1)^\ell$. Put

$$
H=\lceil\log_2N\rceil,\qquad K=2^H,\qquad D=H+d.
\tag{OCC.23}
$$

Pad by $K-N$ fixed $A$ blocks and insert these actual blocks at the
ordered public frontier of a perfect height-$H$ scaffold in the right
subtree of the original source. There is a correct preparation/reader
on every original variable-shape $\mathcal F_D$ with exactly

$$
|S_D|-(2^m+1)^\ell+1
\tag{OCC.24}
$$

attained complete names, merging exactly this scaffold image among
canonical states and giving every other canonical state its own name.
Its preparation, on every source, has

$$
T_{\rm prep}=2^D-1,\qquad Q_{\max}\le D,\qquad
A_{\rm prep}=(D-1)2^D+1.
\tag{OCC.25}
$$

The reader serves every original request with zero Reads or one actual
owner-root Read of length $H+1\le D$, chosen before reply and count.

Refine the merged name by requiring it also to supply the entire
$\ell$-bit actual gadget phase vector before any late request, preserving
every other assigned name. The refined complete attained alphabet is
exactly

$$
|S_D|-(2^m+1)^\ell+2^\ell.
\tag{OCC.26}
$$

The same paid scan attains this refinement. On the unrefined merged
canonical fiber, any deterministic acquisition that must output all
phases from its original-root Reads needs at least $\ell$ Reads on
every source in that canonical fiber. Exactly $\ell$ Reads attain
this descriptor task by querying one fixed actual $x$ owner per
gadget. These are descriptor-acquisition bounds under the named fiber,
not extra Reads beyond (OCC.25) or bounds for optimized $M_1(D)$.

Proof. The fixed ordered scaffold is injective on its frontier tuple
and belongs to $S_D$. The native lift is bijective, so its canonical
image has exactly $(2^m+1)^\ell$ states. A common finite membership
table gives them one name and all other $S_D$ states distinct names.

Before any request, actually Read every original-root literal $Rq$
with $q\in W_D$, in a public fixed order, including absent replies.
The acquired constructor array computes $u=\pi_D(v)$ and its
membership name for every $T=\langle A,v\rangle\in\mathcal F_D$.
This is the credited paid construction of [OCB, Theorem 3.4][OCB]
and [RRN, Theorem 7.1][RRN]. Each canonical state occurs as an actual
right subtree, so all stated names are attained, proving (OCC.24).
The scan has $2^D-1$ words and

$$
\sum_{j=0}^{D-1}(j+1)2^j=(D-1)2^D+1,
$$

giving (OCC.25). The scan and finite table construction are source-blind
initially, and no request is used during preparation.

At a singleton name every full target factor is already fixed. At the
merged name, targets strictly above the frontier have constant branch
factor, and targets in the padding have the fixed factors of $A$.
Every remaining target has form $Ra_iq$, $q\in W_d$, at a public
actual frontier root $Ra_i$. Variable-owner targets query their own
actual root; selector-owner targets query their own actual root.
A connector uses its variable-owner root for every target except
$q=L$, which uses its selector-owner root. Thus each target's full
factor is decoded from one actual reply at a literal $Ra_j$, with
$|Ra_j|=H+1$. The root choice and table depend only on the name,
$D$ and the request, before the reply and every authentic count.
Targets whose table is constant can use zero Reads. There is never
a joint read of a selector and a variable.

All frontier occurrences are actually present. Homomorphism of pairing
therefore gives

$$
r_{\rho^kT}(Ra_iq)=r_{\rho^k(T|_{Ra_i})}(q).
\tag{OCC.27}
$$

This uses exactly the actual-presence premise of
`NativeDepthPatterns.original_present_transport`; subtree notation is
mathematical identification, not an input port. Canonicalization
preserves the scaffold constructors, every selected owner reply and
every requested full factor on the whole inverse-image fiber, including
variable shapes. Equation (OCC.5) therefore gives every subsequently
supplied authentic-count reply, with no further Reads. The construction
serves all original targets, not merely those at the chosen cut.

Export only a fixed-width encoding of the complete name. Public
allocation and padded finite computation, followed by the paid isolation
service, make the scan array, temporary selectors, control, buffers and
transcripts inaccessible. No seed vector or source-dependent topology
is exported. The code's complete attained cardinality is exactly the
displayed number, even though its fixed-width bit storage can have
unused bit patterns.

For the refinement, compute the phases from the same acquired array
and replace the merged name by its phase-vector names. Every one of
the $2^\ell$ patterns occurs, because both phases of every gadget
are nonempty. Each refined fiber is a subset of the original valid
fiber and can use the same late tables. This proves (OCC.26), which
adds $2^\ell-1$ names to the whole alphabet; it is not a claimed
multiplicative factor for that whole alphabet.

For the descriptor lower bound restrict to actual canonical sources
in the merged fiber, whose unrefined retained name is constant. Any
original-root literal is fixed outside the frontier, lies in padding,
or enters one unique frontier block and hence at most one gadget.
Suppose an acquisition execution never queried a block in gadget $j$.
Change that gadget to any valid opposite-phase tuple, leaving all
others fixed. Every reply in that execution is unchanged. Induction
on the deterministic adaptive path gives the same subsequent queries,
termination and output, contradicting the required different phase
vector. Thus every execution must enter each gadget, requiring at
least $\ell$ Reads. Conversely the root of one fixed $x_i$ owner
in each gadget returns $A$ or $B$ according to its phase, attaining
the task with $\ell$ original-root Reads, each of length $H+1$.
$\square$

